# zip_open with ZIP_CHECKCONS: a Zip64 local header must carry both the
# original and compressed size fields, even when only the uncompressed size
# needs Zip64. Such an entry must open, not be rejected as an invalid Zip64
# extra field.
program tryopen
arguments -s -c test.zip
file test.zip zip64-local-both-sizes.zip
return 0
stdout
opening 'test.zip' succeeded, 1 entries
end-of-inline-data
